# Copy to .env.local. Every setting below is optional: the application runs
# with none of them set, which is what `npm run dev` does.
#
# There is no secret here, and there is no place for one: everything below is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, which means it ships in the browser bundle and is readable by
# anyone. The API's own secrets (SUB_PEPPER, VAULT_KEY_PEPPER) live in the
# Cloudflare Worker and are set with `wrangler secret put`, never in a file
# next to the source. See api/README.md.
#
# With none of these set, the application is the client-only tool: it calls no
# API, has no account and no database, and nothing leaves the browser. Each
# variable below turns on a real data flow, which /legal and /confidentialite
# then declare from these same flags.

# Public base URL, used for canonical links, the sitemap, robots.txt and the
# Open Graph images. Falls back to https://crible.eu.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Domain registered with Plausible, the cookieless analytics used by the site.
# When it is unset, the analytics script is not injected at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=crible.eu

# Base URL of the optional backend (api/, a Cloudflare Worker). It turns on the
# anonymous public counters and the /statistiques page that reads them. Unset,
# the page answers 404 and nothing on the site announces a counter.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CRIBLE_API_URL=https://crible-api.example.workers.dev

# Google OAuth web client id. With the URL above, it turns on the encrypted
# profile vault (sign-in, save, restore). Either one missing leaves the vault
# closed and its cards unrendered.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
